WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:18.123
Anne had become a regular visitor to Miss Lavender's since her first unplanned visit in February.

2
00:00:18.124 --> 00:00:26.851
One morning Anne realized it had been two weeks since her last visit, so she set off through the woods to Miss Lavender's house.

3
00:00:26.852 --> 00:00:32.968
When Anne arrived, Miss Lavender was wearing a deep red dress with a gray shawl.

4
00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:39.980
Anne said merrily, "You look like the queen of the fairies!" Miss Lavender smiled warmly.

5
00:00:39.981 --> 00:00:45.338
The two of them enjoyed a delicious meal and then sat by the fire.

6
00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:54.731
"I'm glad you're here, Anne. Did anyone ever tell you anything about Stephen Irving and me?" Miss Lavender asked.

7
00:00:54.732 --> 00:01:01.189
"Yes," said Anne truthfully, "I heard you and he were engaged once."

8
00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:08.643
"So we were . . . 25 years ago—a lifetime ago," said Miss Lavender.

9
00:01:08.644 --> 00:01:12.794
"We were supposed to get married the next spring.

10
00:01:12.795 --> 00:01:19.370
I even had my wedding dress made, although nobody but my mother and Stephen ever knew that."

11
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:22.874
"What went wrong?" asked Anne.

12
00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:28.484
"We had just a stupid, silly quarrel," said Miss Lavender.

13
00:01:28.485 --> 00:01:32.398
"So ordinary, I don't even remember how it began.

14
00:01:32.399 --> 00:01:39.687
After the fight Stephen tried to apologize, but I was still sulking, and I wasn't ready to forgive him.

15
00:01:39.688 --> 00:01:44.812
By the time I was ready to forgive him, it was too late.

16
00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:50.252
Stephen was too proud to come back a second time, and I was too proud to go to him.

17
00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:55.680
So it seems our pride and our anger got in the way of our happiness, Anne.

18
00:01:55.681 --> 00:02:02.461
My heart broke when I realized that Stephen Irving was not coming back," the older woman went on.

19
00:02:02.462 --> 00:02:07.932
"But, Anne, a broken heart in real life isn't half as dreadful as it is in books.

20
00:02:07.933 --> 00:02:11.920
It's more like a toothache!" Miss Lavender smiled.

21
00:02:11.921 --> 00:02:17.585
"I'm really a happy person in spite of my broken heart."

22
00:02:17.586 --> 00:02:26.161
After a short silence, Miss Lavender said, "It gave me a shock to hear about Stephen's son that first day you were here, Anne.

23
00:02:26.162 --> 00:02:28.857
What sort of boy is he?"

24
00:02:28.858 --> 00:02:38.771
"Paul Irving is the dearest, sweetest child I ever knew, and he pretends things too, like you and me," Anne replied.

25
00:02:38.772 --> 00:02:44.302
"I'd like to see him," said Miss Lavender softly, as if she was talking to herself.

26
00:02:44.303 --> 00:02:51.494
"Though it might be too painful if he looked too much like Stephen . . . or if he didn't look enough like him.

27
00:02:51.495 --> 00:02:55.699
Anne, please bring him here in a month."

28
00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.816
A month later Anne and Paul walked through the woods to the stone house.

29
00:03:00.817 --> 00:03:03.905
They met Miss Lavender in the lane.

30
00:03:03.906 --> 00:03:08.406
"So this is Stephen's boy," she said, looking at Paul.

31
00:03:08.407 --> 00:03:12.882
"He . . . he is very like his father."

32
00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:17.768
"Everyone says I'm a chip off the old block!" said Paul confidently.

33
00:03:17.769 --> 00:03:25.219
Miss Lavender smiled and seemed to quickly put aside her feelings of sadness over her old romance.

34
00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:35.020
For the rest of the afternoon, Miss Lavender entertained Paul as if he was anybody's son, and they all had a very enjoyable afternoon together.

35
00:03:35.021 --> 00:03:42.355
As Anne walked Paul home, Paul announced, "I like Miss Lavender! And I like her house too!"

36
00:03:42.356 --> 00:03:51.237
Over the next few months, Paul visited Miss Lavender several times, and they became friends.

37
00:03:51.238 --> 00:03:56.352
Spring had arrived, and Anne was walking down the main road of Avonlea.

38
00:03:56.353 --> 00:03:59.726
She saw a small boy and a man walking toward her.

39
00:03:59.727 --> 00:04:03.104
The small boy ran up; it was Paul Irving.

40
00:04:03.105 --> 00:04:08.042
"Oh, Miss Shirley!" Paul said excitedly to Anne. "Guess who's here!

41
00:04:08.043 --> 00:04:14.277
Father is here! Father, this is my beautiful teacher, Miss Shirley."

42
00:04:14.278 --> 00:04:17.982
Stephen Irving came forward to meet Anne with a smile.

43
00:04:17.983 --> 00:04:21.363
He was a tall, older, handsome man.

44
00:04:21.364 --> 00:04:26.654
"Paul wrote about you in his letters," said Mr. Irving with a hearty handshake.

45
00:04:26.655 --> 00:04:30.978
"Miss Shirley, I want to thank you for being Paul's teacher and friend.

46
00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:36.704
And in Paul's last letter he mentioned visiting an old . . . friend of mine.

47
00:04:36.705 --> 00:04:41.514
Do you know Miss Lavender well?" Mr. Irving asked quietly.

48
00:04:41.515 --> 00:04:46.140
"Yes, she is a very close friend of mine," Anne replied.

49
00:04:46.141 --> 00:04:49.694
"I wonder how much you know," he said.

50
00:04:49.695 --> 00:04:53.719
"I know all about it," replied Anne promptly.

51
00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.964
"Anne," Mr. Irving said, "I would like to see Miss Lavender.

52
00:04:57.965 --> 00:05:01.268
Could you ask her if I might visit?"

53
00:05:01.269 --> 00:05:04.855
The next day Anne relayed Mr. Irving's request.

54
00:05:04.856 --> 00:05:09.852
Miss Lavender calmly agreed, saying "He's only an old friend."

55
00:05:09.853 --> 00:05:14.278
But her eyes were twinkling, and she seemed to smile to herself.

56
00:05:14.279 --> 00:05:22.120
A few days later, Anne was on Miss Lavender's porch when Stephen Irving walked up the garden path.

57
00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:29.174
"This house looks the same as it did 25 years ago," he said, looking around with delighted eyes.

58
00:05:29.175 --> 00:05:34.571
"Time stands still in an enchanted place," said Anne seriously.

59
00:05:34.572 --> 00:05:38.555
"When the prince arrives, things begin to happen."

60
00:05:38.556 --> 00:05:45.413
Mr. Irving smiled a little sadly. "Sometimes the prince comes too late, Anne."

61
00:05:45.414 --> 00:05:51.134
Mr. Irving walked up the stone stairs and went into the parlor to talk with Miss Lavender.

62
00:05:51.135 --> 00:05:56.425
One hour later, Anne was sitting on the porch with Charlotte, Miss Lavender's servant,

63
00:05:56.426 --> 00:06:00.987
when she noticed Mr. Irving and Miss Lavender strolling around the garden.

64
00:06:00.988 --> 00:06:07.086
Mr. Irving's arm was around Miss Lavender's waist. This was a good sign!

65
00:06:07.087 --> 00:06:16.189
After another half hour of anxious waiting, Miss Lavender and Mr. Irving came to the porch and happily announced they were engaged.

66
00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:21.208
Anne and Charlotte were overjoyed, for the love between the couple was obvious.

67
00:06:21.209 --> 00:06:32.775
When Mr. Irving told his son, Paul said proudly, "I knew Father would pick a wonderful second mother."
